     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"With no defences the attack succeeds: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, then pivot_internal (not segmented), auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc (stolen_admin), auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. So zero controls is not enough. Both exfiltration paths need admin_db or admin_fileserver. Each of those needs a foothold from auth_db or auth_fileserver, which require stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin comes only from dump_dbadmin_dc, which needs admin_dc. admin_dc needs foothold_dc, and the only source of foothold_dc is auth_dc, which requires NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore blocks foothold_dc, then admin_dc, then stolen_dbadmin, then both database and fileserver footholds, so exfiltration is impossible. The minimum is 1.\"}"
